# ===========================================================================
# Toolkit output — NEVER COMMIT
# These folders and files contain discovered tenant configuration and, in
# -Detailed / audit modes, item-level metadata (file names, UPNs, site URLs).
# Default output goes to C:\PurviewDiscovery (outside the repo); this is a
# backstop for when -OutputRoot is redirected into the repo or a test/mock
# harness runs in-tree.
# ===========================================================================

# Per-run output folders (matched at any depth)
SourceDiscovery-*/
ContentInventory-*/
AuditSample-*/
Comparison-*/

# Output file types produced by the toolkit (safety net).
# The repo itself is .ps1 + .md + LICENSE, so these don't touch tracked source.
*.csv
*.json
*.clixml
*.html
*.zip
*.log

# To intentionally ship a SYNTHETIC sample artifact (never one with real data),
# force-add it past these rules:
#   git add -f examples/sample-report.html
# ...or add a scoped negation, e.g.:
#   !examples/*.html

# ===========================================================================
# OS / editor noise
# ===========================================================================
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
*.swp
*~
